  note={
    Develops NOAL, a statically typed applicative object-oriented language used
    as a vehicle for formal specification and verification with behavioral
    subtyping.
    NOAL has no assignment or mutable state and supports generic invocation
    through run-time overloading on argument types, amounting to an early pure
    functional treatment of multiple dispatch.
