  note={
    Comprehensive type-theoretic treatment of programming-language semantics,
    organized around static and dynamic semantics for individual language
    features.
    Chapter 17 develops data abstraction through existential types, with
    packages as implementations and opening as the client-side elimination
    form.
    Particularly relevant for the way existential elimination reverses the
    apparent scope relationship: an implementation chooses a hidden
    representation type, while opening the package introduces a fresh abstract
    type whose scope extends through the client, preventing the representation
    type from escaping.
    A useful formal account of the scope discipline underlying abstract types
    and representation independence.
  }
}

